{"url": "https://www.wright.edu/admissions/international/graduate-application-checklist", "final_url": "https://www.wright.edu/admissions/international/graduate-application-checklist", "status": 200, "method": "http", "fetched": "2026-10-28", "text": "Graduate Application Checklist | Admissions | Wright State University\nSkip to main content\nCalendar\nDirectories\nMaps\nPilot\nWINGS\nApply\nSearch Wright State\nSearch\nMenu\nClose\nMain navigation\nHome\nDegrees & Programs\nAdmissions\nTuition & Aid\nCampus Life\nResearch\nAthletics\nAbout\nSearch Wright State\nSearch\nDegrees & Programs\nAdmissions\nTuition & Aid\nCampus Life\nResearch\nAthletics\nAbout\nCalendar\nDirectories\nMaps\nPilot\nWINGS\nApply\nInternational Admissions\nHome\nWhy Wright State?\nUndergraduate Admission\nAdmission Requirements\nApplication Instructions\nApplication Checklist\nMajors and Minors\nTuition and Fees\nScholarships\nCheck Your Application Status\nGraduate Admission\nAdmission Requirements\nApplication Instructions\nApplication Checklist\nPrograms\nScholarships and Aid\nTuition and Fees\nCheck Your Application Status\nApplication Deadlines\nInternational Transcripts\nVisa\nVisiting Student (Non-Degree) Programs\nInternational Student News\nStaff Directory\nForms\nPayment Options\nBreadcrumb\nHome\nAdmissions\nInternational Admissions\nGraduate Application Checklist\nThe following items are required for graduate admissions to Wright State.\nCheck the Admission Requirements to see if you qualify.\nCreate an account in the Admissions Portal.\nSubmit a copy of your passport information page showing your photo, name, and date of birth.\nComplete the admission application and submit your $70 non-refundable application fee.\nRefer to the Required Documents section to find a list of missing documents. Upload your documents in either PDF or JPEG format.\nSubmit your complete, official academic record from each college or university previously attended including individual semester transcripts if applicable. A certified English translation must be attached to official foreign transcripts or mark sheets.\nSubmit an official confirmation of your bachelor's degree\nSubmit evidence of your English proficiency. See the admissions requirements for details.\nSubmit your official Graduate Management Admissions Test (GMAT) score or Graduate Record Examination (GRE) score if required for your program. Official test scores must come directly from the testing service. Wright State University's institution code is 1179.\nSubmit your letters of recommendations if required by your program.\nComplete your I20 request from the application portal.\nSubmit your statement of objectives if required by program.\nUniversity Mega Footer\nFirst Column\nColleges & Schools\nBusiness, Raj Soin College of\nEngineering and Computer Science\nGraduate Studies\nHealth, Education, and Human Services\nLake Campus\nLiberal Arts\nMedicine, Boonshoft School of\nScience and Mathematics\nAcademics\nAcademic Calendar\nCatalog\nInformation For\nAlumni\nAthletics\nSecond Column\nAbout Wright State\nAccreditation\nNews\nQuick Facts\nRankings\nStrategic Plan\nCompliance\nConsumer Information\nNon-Discrimination Policy\nSenate Bill 1\nStudent Right to Know\nTitle IX\nThird Column\nResources\nCalendar\nDirectories\nMaps\nPilot\nSmugMug\nWINGS\nServices\nCounseling and Wellness\nDisability Services\nEnrollment Services\nHuman Resources\nLibraries\nParking\nSchedule a Visit\nLake Campus\nFooter\nA-Z Index\nApply\nEmployment\nMake a Gift\nWright State Cares\nContact Information\n3640 Colonel Glenn Hwy.\nDayton, OH 45435 USA\n937-775-1000\nFacebook\nInstagram\nLinkedIn\nTikTok\nYouTube\nAdmissions, Undergraduate\nLocation\n141 Student Union\nHours\nMonday\u2013Friday 8:30 a.m.\u20135 p.m.\nPhone\n937-775-5700\nEmail\nadmissions@wright.edu\nAdmissions, Graduate\nLocation\n160 University Hall\nHours\nMonday-Friday, 8:30 a.m.-5 p.m.\nPhone\n937-775-2976\nFax\n937-775-2453\nEmail\nwsugrad@wright.edu\nCopyr